; Regression: SCALY_POISON in the environment turns the runtime's poison mode
; on by itself (root_pages.poison_from_env, read by the first bucket a
; process creates): a released page reads 0xDD at once.
;
; Before 2026-09-30 only a program that called Page.enable_poison() itself
; got it -- the dazzle, onsgmls and tscaly drivers did; the http, json,
; compress, pg, redis and tls suites set the variable for test programs that
; never read it, so every gate of theirs that said "under poison" ran without.
; The same binary without the variable prints FAIL (the byte stays 7).
; run-env: SCALY_POISON=1

let keep Page.allocate_page()
let p Page.allocate_page()
let raw p as pointer[u8]
*(raw + 100) := 7
Page.release_page(p)
if *(raw + 100) = 0xDD
    print "PASS"
else
    print "FAIL"
